<div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-4">
  <h1>Students</h1>
  <span class="badge bg-secondary fs-6"><%= @students.count %> students</span>
</div>

<p class="lead text-muted mb-4">
  Welcome to the UCF Course Manager. This is Module 1, demonstrating basic Rails concepts
  with in-memory data storage.
</p>

<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-striped table-hover">
    <thead class="table-dark">
      <tr>
        <th>Student Number</th>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Email</th>
        <th>Major</th>
        <th>Actions</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <%#
        ERB (Embedded Ruby) uses <% %> for Ruby code and <%= %> to output
        Java equivalent: JSTL <c:forEach items="${students}" var="student">
        C equivalent: for loop iterating through array of structs
      %>
      <% @students.each do |student| %>
        <tr>
          <td><code><%= student.student_number %></code></td>
          <td><%= student.full_name %></td>
          <td><%= mail_to student.email, student.email %></td>
          <td><%= student.major %></td>
          <td>
            <%= link_to "View", student_path(student.id), class: "btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="card bg-light mt-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h5 class="card-title">Module 1 Notes</h5>
    <ul class="mb-0">
      <li>Students are stored <strong>in memory</strong> using a Ruby class</li>
      <li>Data will be lost when the server restarts</li>
      <li>In Module 2, we'll connect to PostgreSQL for persistent storage</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
